    "q-32989": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32989",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(6,0,2)$ and $B(1,1,3)$, and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨3,1,-2⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨3,1,-2⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,1,3⟩-⟨6,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $a=⟨6,0,2⟩$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\ r & =⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨3,1,-2⟩+t⟨-5,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
