    "q-33819": {
      "dom_id": "step-q33819",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 23 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and $w=⟨4,7,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-33i+13j-41k \\\\  & =⟨-33,13,-41⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-33,13,-41⟩.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
