    "q-70975": {
      "dom_id": "step-q70975",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨0,8,-1⟩+t⟨-1,1,7⟩+s⟨3,-5,1⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-1,1,7⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-5,1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =36i+22j+2k \\\\  & =⟨36,22,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨36,22,2⟩.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
